#!/usr/bin/env python3
# revert_tma2_experiments.py — marker TMA2_EXPERIMENTS_REVERT_20261016
#
# Removes the three falsified TMA_V2 backtest experiments, cleanly:
#   TMA2_PARTIAL_TP_20261014       partial profit booking (T1 / T2)
#   TMA2_SL_CLOSE_CONFIRM_20261016 close-basis SL + entry confirmation
#   TMA2_DECAY_ROLL_20261016       decay roll (wide / no SL on the new leg)
#
# BACKEND  backtest_tma_v2_runner.py and tma_v2_engine.py are restored to the
#   exact pre-partial-TP versions (embedded below, sha-checked) — but only if
#   each file is one of the known patched states (partial / + SL-close /
#   + roll); a hand-edited file aborts the whole revert.
# FRONTEND exact inverse of each patch's edits, newest first (roll →
#   SL-close → partial), only for the patches actually present. Kept on
#   purpose: the TMA_V2 diag block in the CSV export (added by the partial
#   patch, useful for every TMA_V2 run) — its comment is re-worded.
# FILES    deleted: test_tma2_partial_tp.py, test_tma2_sl_close_confirm.py,
#   test_tma2_decay_roll.py and every .bak-<one of the three fences>.
#   Safety copies of everything touched go to
#   ~/.scalp-app/patch_backups/TMA2_EXPERIMENTS_REVERT_<timestamp>/.
#   Mirrored to desktop/src-tauri/{backend,frontend}/ when those trees exist.
# Gates: py_compile, esbuild parse, no trace of the three fences left in the
#   targets, then the TMA_V2 engine, DTE-lots, live signal engine, live core,
#   VAP engine and lot-compounding suites. Any failure → every file restored.
#
# Afterwards: saved / queued configs that still carry s1.partial, s1.roll,
# sl_trigger or entry_confirm_bars run as the sealed strategy (the keys are
# ignored). Past runs and their exports are untouched.
#
# Usage: python3 revert_tma2_experiments.py [--repo PATH] [--allow-dirty] [--skip-tests]

